        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پاسگاه",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پاسگاه (pâsgâh) — \"a police post; a guard post\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در جاده یک پاسگاه پلیس بود. Dar jâdde yek pâsgâh-e polis bud. There was a police post on the road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pâs 'watch, guard' + gâh 'place'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pâsgâh is a native compound of pâs 'watch, guard', the word behind pâsbân 'guard', and gâh 'place'. EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
